course: dictionary
lesson: 8921
title: Siege: a castle under attack
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A siege is when an army surrounds a town or castle, blocks the roads, and stops food and help from getting in. The people inside are trapped, and the attackers hope they will run out of food and give up. Read the words around siege to find its meaning: «The army stayed outside the castle walls for months.»
explain: Look for the clues. Army, walls, outside, months and food all point to a siege. Now swap your meaning into the sentence: "The army stayed outside the walls for months, stopping food getting in" makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Siege can also be a picture. «Your body is a castle under siege by germs too small to see.» Under siege means attacked or troubled from all sides. Germs cannot really bring an army, but the picture helps you feel how hard the fight is.
explain: Siege can also mean police surrounding a building where someone is hiding. In the news, «a police siege» means police wait outside while a person is trapped inside. The clue words are surrounded, trapped and waiting. If a word still puzzles you, check a dictionary.
fact: A siege is when an army surrounds a place so that food and help cannot get in.
fact: «Under siege» means attacked or troubled from all sides, as in «Your body is a castle under siege by germs».
fact: «Lay siege to» means to start a siege, and «lift the siege» means to end one.
fact: In December 1240 the Mongol army under Batu took Kyiv after a siege; much of the city was ruined, but it survived as a smaller town.
fact: In cartoons a castle under siege is full of catapults and fighting, but in real life attackers often just waited for weeks until the defenders ran out of food.
exercise: «The army surrounded the castle and stopped food getting in for months.» What is a siege? | A big feast held in a castle hall | *An army surrounds a place to stop food and help getting in | A fast boat on a river | A party for the king's birthday
exercise: «Your body is a castle under siege by germs.» What does under siege mean here? | Sleeping soundly | *Attacked or troubled from all sides | Made of thick grey stone | Tidied up and cleaned
exercise: Police wait outside a house where a man is hiding inside. Which words best name this? | A pirate ship battle | A quiet picnic in the park | A parade through the town | *A police siege
test: «The Mongol army took Kyiv after a siege in 1240, but the city survived.» What does siege mean in this sentence? | *An army blocking a city so food and help cannot get in | A long holiday by the sea | A fast river crossing
test: Which phrase means to start a siege? | lift the siege | a siege tower | *lay siege to
exam: Ella says a siege is a kind of castle. What is the best answer? | *No, a siege is what an army does when it surrounds a place to stop food and help getting in | Yes, a siege is a tall tower where the king lives | No, a siege is a quiet picnic | Yes, a siege is a kind of dog
